{"metadata":{"role":"article","modules":[{"name":"LinkerSets"}],"title":"Unique keys","roleHeading":"Article"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets"]]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/linkersets\/uniquekeys"]}],"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"kind":"article","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/UniqueKeys","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Records are anonymous bytes in a section, and the linker concatenates them, so two modules can"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"register the same route or the same event name, and nothing notices until the program reads the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"set. The linker does refuse two definitions of one symbol. A record declared with a unique key gets"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a function beside it whose symbol is named for the record’s kind and the key, so a second"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"declaration of that kind and key defines the symbol again and the build fails, naming it."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["enum Routes {","    @LinkerSetEntry(kind: 0x726F_7574, uniqueKey: \"\/home\")","    static let home = Route(path: \"\/home\")","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/LinkerSetEntry(kind:uniqueKey:)"},{"type":"text","text":" takes the key as a string literal. A client’s own macro gives"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each declaration its key from LinkerSetsMacroSupport’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"uniqueKey(of:attribute:)"},{"type":"text","text":": from the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"declaration, such as an event type’s name, or from an argument of the attribute through"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"uniqueKeyArgument(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":". Records of different kinds never clash, because the kind is part of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"symbol’s name."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"What the developer sees","type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"What-the-developer-sees"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The symbol reads ","type":"text"},{"code":"$linkerset_kind_<kind>_key_<key>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": the kind as eight hex digits, then the key,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with ASCII letters and digits as they are and every other UTF-8 byte as ","type":"text"},{"code":"_","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and two hex digits. The","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"route above is ","type":"text"},{"code":"$linkerset_kind_726F7574_key__2Fhome","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and an event named ","type":"text"},{"code":"OrderPlaced","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" of kind","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"\"evnt\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"code":"$linkerset_kind_65766E74_key_OrderPlaced","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Two declarations in one module are caught by the compiler:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["error: multiple definitions of symbol '$linkerset_kind_726F7574_key__2Fhome'"],"syntax":null,"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Two modules linked into one program are caught by the linker, which names both object files. Each","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"linker words it its own way.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Apple’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ld"},{"type":"text","text":":"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["duplicate symbol '_$linkerset_kind_65766E74_key_OrderPlaced' in:","    ...\/libCheckout.a[2](OrderPlaced.swift.o)","    ...\/libOrders.a[2](OrderPlaced.swift.o)","ld: 1 duplicate symbols"],"syntax":null,"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"LLVM’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"lld","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for ELF, which Bazel links with on Linux and Android uses, points at the macro","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"expansion that declares each one:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["ld.lld: error: duplicate symbol: $linkerset_kind_65766E74_key_OrderPlaced",">>> defined at @__swiftmacro_6Orders11OrderPlaced5EventfMp_.swift:6",">>>            OrderPlaced.swift.o:($linkerset_kind_65766E74_key_OrderPlaced) in archive libOrders.a",">>> defined at @__swiftmacro_8Checkout11OrderPlaced5EventfMp_.swift:6",">>>            OrderPlaced.swift.o:(.text.$linkerset_kind_65766E74_key_OrderPlaced+0x0) in archive libCheckout.a"],"syntax":null,"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"GNU gold, which ","type":"text"},{"code":"swiftc","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" links with on Linux by default:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["\/usr\/bin\/ld.gold: error: .\/libCheckout.a(OrderPlaced.swift.o): multiple definition of '$linkerset_kind_65766E74_key_OrderPlaced'","\/usr\/bin\/ld.gold: .\/libOrders.a(OrderPlaced.swift.o): previous definition here"],"syntax":null,"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"wasm-ld"},{"type":"text","text":", for WebAssembly:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["wasm-ld: error: duplicate symbol: $linkerset_kind_65766E74_key_OrderPlaced",">>> defined in ...\/Orders.objlib\/a.o",">>> defined in ...\/Checkout.objlib\/b.o"],"syntax":null,"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"On Windows, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"lld-link"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"link.exe"},{"text":" refuse a symbol defined twice as well (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LNK2005"},{"text":" from","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"link.exe"},{"text":"), but no test shows it yet.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"One linked image at a time","type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"One-linked-image-at-a-time"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The check covers the modules linked statically into one executable or one shared library. It","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"doesn’t reach across images:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Shared libraries and frameworks keep their symbols apart. On Apple platforms each image’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"symbols live in a namespace of their own, and on ELF the first definition the loader finds wins","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"without an error. The function is internal, so a library doesn’t export it either.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A library opened with ","type":"text"},{"code":"dlopen","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is never compared with the program.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A record of the same key in another image is still read, so a client that needs the guarantee for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the whole process keeps a check at run time too, such as throwing when two records share a name.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Static archives","type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"Static-archives"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A static archive’s member is linked only when something references it. Its record and its key’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"symbol sit in the same object file, so the two are linked together or not at all: a module whose"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"records are missing (see "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/PlatformsAndLinking","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":") is missing from the check as well."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"SwiftPM and Bazel link a target’s modules whole, and there a duplicate is an error. Apple’s "},{"code":"ld","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"makes one exception: with "},{"code":"-dead_strip","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", the default for release builds in Xcode, a duplicate from"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"an archive member read on demand is only a warning, "},{"code":"ld: warning: duplicate symbol","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and the link"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"succeeds. Link the archive whole ("},{"code":"-force_load","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", or "},{"code":"-all_load","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" for every archive), or make the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"linker’s warnings errors with "},{"code":"-Xlinker -fatal_warnings","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", to keep it an error. Linux’s linkers and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"wasm-ld","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" make it an error either way."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Where a key can’t be checked","type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"Where-a-key-cant-be-checked"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A symbol declared inside a ","type":"text"},{"code":"private","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"fileprivate","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" type, or an extension marked either way, is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"local to its file, and the linker never compares local symbols. The macros refuse a unique key","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"there: “can’t check its unique key inside a private or fileprivate type”. The enclosing type can be","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"seen from swift-syntax 600 on. With an older swift-syntax the key in such a type compiles and goes","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"unchecked. A key that is empty, or a ","type":"text"},{"code":"uniqueKey:","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" argument that isn’t a string literal or holds an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"interpolation, is refused too (","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/WhatTheMacrosRefuse","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":").","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"What is tested where","type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"What-is-tested-where"},{"rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Format","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Covered by","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Runs in","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Mach-O, macOS","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Tests\/CompileFailures"},{"type":"text","text":": "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DuplicateEventNames"},{"type":"text","text":" (an archive read on demand), "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DistinctEventNames"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DuplicateKeyInOneModule"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"just test","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"ELF, Linux"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The same tests, linked with ","type":"text"},{"code":"lld","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; gold checked by hand","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"CI’s Linux Bazel job","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"WebAssembly","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Checked by hand with the 6.4.3 SDK’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"wasm-ld"},{"type":"text","text":"; "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UniqueKeyRecordTests"},{"type":"text","text":" reads keyed records"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"just wasi-test","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"COFF, Windows"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Untested: ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UniqueKeyRecordTests"},{"text":" shows keyed records build and read, but no test links a duplicate","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"CI’s Windows workflow","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]]],"type":"table","header":"row"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The Bazel tests build their programs with ","type":"text"},{"code":"tools\/link_test.bzl","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which links outside Bazel’s own","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"link step so that a link meant to fail doesn’t fail the build. SwiftPM can’t hold such a test: a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"package with a duplicate fails to build as a whole.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Guides","identifiers":["doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/DeclaringAKind","doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/FindingRecords","doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/WhatTheMacrosRefuse","doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/ReplacingARegistry","doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/PlatformsAndLinking","doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/Performance"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Guides"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Make two records of one kind with the same key fail to build, within one executable or library."}],"references":{"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/FindingRecords":{"title":"Finding records","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/FindingRecords","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Read every declaration of a kind, as the type you expect."}],"url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/findingrecords","type":"topic","role":"article","kind":"article"},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/PlatformsAndLinking":{"title":"Platforms and linking","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/PlatformsAndLinking","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Where records are found, how, and which test shows it."}],"url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/platformsandlinking","type":"topic","role":"article","kind":"article"},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/WhatTheMacrosRefuse":{"title":"What the macros refuse","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/WhatTheMacrosRefuse","abstract":[{"text":"Every declaration a record can’t describe is a compile error, with a message that says why.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/whatthemacrosrefuse","type":"topic","role":"article","kind":"article"},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets":{"title":"LinkerSets","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/linkersets","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Declarations that register themselves at compile time and are found at run time across every module a program links."}],"role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets"},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/Performance":{"title":"Performance","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/Performance","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"What records cost as an app grows: nothing at launch, a walk of the records when a set is read,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and a few milliseconds of build time per marked declaration."}],"url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/performance","type":"topic","role":"article","kind":"article"},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/DeclaringAKind":{"url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/declaringakind","role":"article","type":"topic","title":"Declaring a kind","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/DeclaringAKind","kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Pick the number that tags your declarations, and decide whether your users write it."}]},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/LinkerSetEntry(kind:uniqueKey:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/linkersetentry(kind:uniquekey:)","role":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"LinkerSetEntry(kind:uniqueKey:)","fragments":[{"text":"macro","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"LinkerSetEntry","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"kind","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"UInt32","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s6UInt32V"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"uniqueKey","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/LinkerSetEntry(kind:uniqueKey:)","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Declares a record of ","type":"text"},{"code":"kind","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" whose value is this declaration’s, and that no other record of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"kind","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in the same executable or library may share ","type":"text"},{"code":"uniqueKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with.","type":"text"}]},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/ReplacingARegistry":{"role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/replacingaregistry","kind":"article","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/ReplacingARegistry","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Move a central list of event types, routes or registrations onto declarations that find"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"themselves."}],"title":"Replacing a hand-written registry"}}}